mindmap
  root((Lesson 22))
    Vocabulary p1-p4
      dream
        Core: a dream; an ambition
        Pattern: of/about + sb/sth
        Pattern: of/about + doing
        Pattern: that + clause
        Pattern: daydream about
        Example: never dreamed of receiving
        Watch out: two senses, read the context
      age
        Core: how old somebody is
        Ask: How old is ...?
        Ask: What's ... age?
        Pattern: at the age of + number
        Pattern: of one's own age
        Extended: era, period
        Extended: for ages, a long time
      channel
        Core: sea channel
        Note: the Channel takes a capital C
        Extended: duct, waterway
        Extended: fairway, sea route
        Extended: customs lane
        Extended: TV channel
        Confusable: Chanel, the brand
      throw
        Core: to throw, to toss
        Forms: threw - thrown
        Pattern: throw sth away
        Pattern: throw sth into
        Pattern: throw sth to sb, direction
        Pattern: throw sth at sb, target
        Example: threw the bottle into the sea
    Grammar p8-p10
      Core ideas of prepositions
        of: a link between two things
        from: leaving a starting point
        in: inside, within a frame
        on: on top of, contact surface
      Verb + preposition = phrasal verb
        Works like a transitive verb
        Object follows directly
        Verb after a preposition takes -ing
      Verb + of
        consist of, to be made up of
        hear of, to hear about
      Verb + from
        benefit from, to gain from
        suffer from, to be troubled by
      Verb + in
        believe in, to trust
        fill in, to complete a form
      Verb + on
        call on, to visit
        focus on, to concentrate on
        concentrate on
      Verb = verb + preposition
        fight = fight against
      Verb + noun + preposition
        pay attention to
        An adjective can come before the noun
    Text p4-p7
      Seven sentences
        1 Past simple: never dreamed of receiving
        2 Past continuous + past simple: were travelling and put
        3 Past simple: threw into the sea
        4 Past simple: ten months later received
        5 Present simple: write regularly now
        6 Present perfect: have decided to use
        7 Future simple: will cost and will travel
      Linking words
        and: background first, point second
        but: the point comes after it
        However: contrast, followed by a comma
        both and each other: mutual action
      Review
        L21: it came into use
        L14: Neither of us spoke
